objects.desc:
A steel law for the fibres of a section, from the Law menu. Stresses in kN/m2, strains dimensionless.
Steel01 - bilinear with kinematic hardening (the default);
Steel02 - Giuffre-Menegotto-Pinto: the same, with a smooth elastic to plastic transition;
ReinforcingSteel - a reinforcing bar, with a strain-hardening branch to its ultimate strength.

A steel law for the fibres of a section, from the Law menu. Stresses in kN/m2, strains dimensionless.
Steel01 - bilinear with kinematic hardening (the default);
Steel02 - Giuffre-Menegotto-Pinto: the same, with a smooth elastic to plastic transition;
ReinforcingSteel - a reinforcing bar, with a strain-hardening branch to its ultimate strength.

A law that is neither concrete nor steel, for the fibres of a section, from the Law menu. Stresses in kN/m2, strains dimensionless.
ElasticPP - elastic, then perfectly plastic (the default);
Hysteretic - a bilinear or trilinear backbone, each side of its own, with pinching and damage;
Elastic - linear, to a rupture strain if you give one: a carbon or glass fibre laminate, a tendon.
